    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Send a Telegram alert for every wallet transfer\n\n### How it works\nThe Qersh app on the merchant's phone posts every incoming wallet transfer (Vodafone Cash, Orange Cash, e& money, InstaPay) to the Qersh Trigger as a signed JSON delivery; the trigger verifies the signature and refuses anything else with 401. The connection test gets no message. A new transfer is remembered by delivery_id in a Data table, so the phone's retries never send the alert twice; then a Telegram message goes out with the amount, payer, wallet, transaction id and risk. A later \"suspected forgery\" verdict sends a warning so nobody ships against that money.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add your **Qersh Webhook API** credential (install the Qersh community node first; on n8n Cloud open the nodes panel, \"More from the community\").\n2. In Settings, put the chat id that should get the alerts (send /start to your bot, then read the chat id from the Telegram Trigger). Select your Telegram bot credential in both Telegram nodes.\n3. Create a Data table qersh_deliveries with the text columns delivery_id, transfer_id, amount, currency, payer, received_at and select it in both Data table nodes.\n4. Activate the workflow, copy the trigger's **Production URL** into the Qersh app (More, Wallets, Add wallet, \"your store URL\"), then paste the key the phone shows into the credential. \"Test connection\" on the phone must say the signature was verified.\n\n### Customization tips\nMessages are English; translate the two texts freely and keep the digits Latin. Add a message for transfers that need a human check (auto_confirm_ok is false).\n\nQersh (Qersh Pay) is a wallet notification relay, not a payment service provider. Docs: https://qersh.cfd/en/integrations/n8n",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 1
      },
